\title{Computable Specifications}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-03-11}

\p{
    In the first few months of 2026, most of work has been on [CompPoly](https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/CompPoly), a formally verified
    model of computable polynomials in Lean.
    The purpose of CompPoly is to provide a computable base for the specs in [Arklib](https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/ArkLib).
}

\p{
    Why make a formal specification computable? A formal specification is a description of the correct computational behavior of a program.
    The propositions comprising a specification become more and more expressive and accurate as they incorporate computational primitives.
    What then is the most accurate description of correct program behavior?
    \em{A correct program.}
}